  <string id="st_bm_uniq_ammo_gauss_descr">
    <text>Ammo for the electromagnetic rifle. Extremely rare. We found it and do not even know where. Buy it while it lasts.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_ammo_gauss_name">
    <text>Gauss rounds (5 pcs.)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_agr_descr">
    <text>Magnetic pass to the Agroprom underground. Its former owner will not be going back.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_agr_name">
    <text>Access card: AGROPROM</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_jup_descr">
    <text>Pass to the Jupiter underground. Those who brought it out split the price evenly and never came back.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_jup_name">
    <text>Access card: Jupiter</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_x18_descr">
    <text>Electronic key to Lab X-18. Retrieved from Dark Valley; better not ask at what cost.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_card_x18_name">
    <text>Access card: X-18</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_csky_descr">
    <text>The Clear Sky exoskeleton is one of the oldest in the Zone. Restored to factory condition.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_csky_name">
    <text>Clear Sky exoskeleton CH-5</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_greh_descr">
    <text>An exoskeleton bearing the Sin insignia: heavy, armored, uncompromising. Bullets cannot stop it, and neither can conscience.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_greh_name">
    <text>Sin exoskeleton</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_isg_descr">
    <text>ISG combat exoskeleton. It reached us outside every channel; not everyone can wear one.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_exo_isg_name">
    <text>ISG exoskeleton</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_gauss_descr">
    <text>Experimental electromagnetic rifle. Ammunition is a separate problem.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_gauss_name">
    <text>Gauss rifle</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_hyena_descr">
    <text>It is sitting here as if waiting for its owner. Thanks for the lot.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_hyena_name">
    <text>Hyena</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_kar98_hunter_descr">
    <text>The Forester made this restored Mauser with Japanese March optics. He says it is for hunting trespassers in the Red Forest.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_kar98_hunter_name">
    <text>Mauser Kar98 Retrotac</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_karatysh_descr">
    <text>A shortened PKM with Zenit attachments. Machine-gun firepower in an assault-rifle-sized package.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_karatysh_name">
    <text>PKM Karatysh</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m24_green_descr">
    <text>Military sniper rifle in green camouflage. Its former owner changed professions forever.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m24_green_name">
    <text>M24 in green camouflage</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m82_descr">
    <text>Large-caliber semi-automatic rifle. It punches through anything you find in the Zone. Do not ask where it came from.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m82_name">
    <text>Barrett M82</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m98b_descr">
    <text>High-precision .338 Lapua bolt-action rifle for long-range work. Scope not included.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_m98b_name">
    <text>Barrett M98B</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_nosorog_monolit_descr">
    <text>A Nosorog marked with Monolith insignia. Taken from those who believed and believe no longer. The delivery cost us three men.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_nosorog_monolit_name">
    <text>Monolith armor</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd47_descr">
    <text>Customized AKM by Rifle Dynamics with ISG attachments. Intercepted with a shipment of gear on the Cordon.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd47_name">
    <text>RD47 AKM (ISG)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd74m_isg_descr">
    <text>Full-size ISG assault rifle from the same batch as the shortened model. Intercepted on a supply route.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd74m_isg_name">
    <text>AK-74M Frost (ISG)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd74u_isg_descr">
    <text>Shortened rifle from an ISG combat unit. The serial number is filed off; no unnecessary questions.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd74u_isg_name">
    <text>AKS-74U Frost (ISG)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd9x39_isg_descr">
    <text>Vintorez modified for the ISG high-powered cartridge. It should not be on the open market, which is why it is here.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rd9x39_isg_name">
    <text>Vintorez 9x39 (ISG)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rsh12_descr">
    <text>12.7 mm assault revolver developed by TsKIB for special operations in confined spaces. Taken from an operative in Limansk.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_rsh12_name">
    <text>RSh-12</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_saiga_isg_descr">
    <text>Tactical Saiga with ISG attachments. It arrived in a shipment that was meant to leave the country, but never did.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_saiga_isg_name">
    <text>Saiga-12 Tactics (ISG)</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_shak12_descr">
    <text>12.7x55 assault system for fighting indoors, where walls offer no protection. From the same batch as the Vykhlop.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_shak12_name">
    <text>ShAK-12</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vintorez_merk_descr">
    <text>Mercenary Vintorez variant: lighter and more ergonomic. The previous owner never completed the contract.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vintorez_merk_name">
    <text>VSS Merk</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vss_savant_descr">
    <text>Upgraded Vintorez with an improved suppressor. The former owner did not live to collect it from the workshop.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vss_savant_name">
    <text>VSS Vintorez M1</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vssk_descr">
    <text>A 12.7 mm large-caliber suppressed sniper rifle, quieter than some Vintorez models. From an arsenal no one guards anymore.</text>
  </string>
  <string id="st_bm_uniq_vssk_name">
    <text>VSSK Vykhlop</text>
  </string>
